.SS "int32_t schultz_arena_init (\fBschultz_arena\fP * arena, size_t block_size)"

.PP
Prepares an arena for use\&. No memory is obtained from the system until the first allocation\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIarena\fP The arena to initialize\&. Must not be NULL\&. Its previous contents are overwritten, so call schultz_arena_free first if it was in use\&. 
.br
\fIblock_size\fP Bytes to request per block\&. Pass 0 to accept the default\&. A single allocation larger than this still succeeds; the arena takes an oversized block for it\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK on success, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when arena is NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void schultz_arena_free (\fBschultz_arena\fP * arena)"

.PP
Releases every block back to the system\&. Every pointer the arena has returned becomes invalid\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIarena\fP The arena to release\&. NULL and an already freed arena are both accepted and do nothing\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void * schultz_arena_alloc (\fBschultz_arena\fP * arena, size_t size, size_t alignment)"

.PP
Allocates aligned, uninitialized memory from the arena\&. The returned memory stays valid until schultz_arena_reset or schultz_arena_free is called on this arena\&. It must never be passed to free()\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIarena\fP The arena to allocate from\&. NULL yields NULL\&. 
.br
\fIsize\fP Bytes to allocate\&. Must be greater than zero\&. 
.br
\fIalignment\fP Required address alignment in bytes\&. Must be a power of two\&. Pass 0 to accept the platform's maximum fundamental alignment, which is correct for any ordinary object\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A pointer to at least size bytes aligned as requested, or NULL when arena is NULL, size is zero, alignment is not a power of two, or the underlying allocation failed\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void schultz_arena_reset (\fBschultz_arena\fP * arena)"

.PP
Makes every prior allocation available again\&. Blocks are kept rather than returned to the system, which is what lets a frame loop settle and stop calling malloc\&. Every pointer the arena has returned becomes invalid\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIarena\fP The arena to reset\&. NULL is accepted and does nothing\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "size_t schultz_arena_used (const \fBschultz_arena\fP * arena)"

.PP
Reports bytes handed out since the last reset\&. Includes bytes lost to alignment padding, so it may exceed the sum of the sizes requested\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIarena\fP The arena to query\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Bytes currently handed out across all blocks\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "size_t schultz_arena_capacity (const \fBschultz_arena\fP * arena)"

.PP
Reports bytes currently held from the system\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIarena\fP The arena to query\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The sum of every block's capacity, whether in use or not\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint32_t schultz_arena_block_count (const \fBschultz_arena\fP * arena)"

.PP
Counts blocks held\&. Useful for asserting that a frame loop has settled: once this stops growing, the arena has stopped calling malloc\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIarena\fP The arena to query\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The number of blocks in the chain\&. 
.RE
.PP

